{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/898221-2e-insert-nameless-orders-here","id":898221,"title":"[2E] Insert Nameless Orders Here","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-24T14:29:33-07:00","id":898221,"title":"[2E] Insert Nameless Orders Here","content":"This one is pretty straightforward. Post any Nameless Orders you've made or translated for Second Edition. I'll start with one of mine.<br /> <br /> <b>The Epistolary Society of Boundless Inquiry</b><br /> <br /> Mages have always been a little more well-traveled than their Sleeper counterparts due to the opportunities created by magic. However, such means were always somewhat cumbersome, and limited to those with access to the Space Arcanum. It was only with the advent of widespead postal services that long-distance correspondence became a popular means of sharing ideas among reclusive scholars. In the same vein as the later epistolary circles of Howard Phillips Lovecraft and his associates, mages with little interest in joining established orders but still craving colleagues with whom to share their love of the Mysteries began to converse through letters.<br /> <br /> The practice expanded to solitaries and apostates of all sorts throughout the United States and Western Europe, and the original writers grew into adepts and masters of the Art. Soon they had more to share such as grimoires and imbued items, and dissertations on their long years of experience with Artifacts and ruins from across national borders. The two Epistolary Societies were separated by an ocean until the telegraph and telephone emerged, and soon messages were being exchanged across the Atlantic too.<br /> <br /> The Society grows with every advance in communication and transportation, and its scattered archives and instructional materials are more accessible than ever. They have, unbeknownst to most, become a legitimate Order in their own right - a decentralized, horizontally organized one with strong values of secrecy and security against outsiders, and limitless development and exchange from within. Left-Handed practices and personal Legacies are being allowed to bloom and spread as casting times and bandwidth permit.<br /> <br /> <b>Order Tools:</b> Cloaks, masks, secret communications, and writing utensils.<br /> <br /> <b>Initiation</b><br /> 1: Investigation (Cryptography)<br /> 2: High Speech<br /> 3: Rote Specialties (Academics, Investigation, Occult)<br /> 4: Library (Occult) 3<br /> 5: Grimoire 3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","user":"Aiden","date":". 05-26-2016, 01:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T14:45:50-07:00","id":898240,"title":"","content":"<b>Children of the moon</b><br /> When wolf blooded awaken they feel disconnected from luna. The children of the moon is small sect of gathered mages who had once expected to under go the first change and strive to remain connected to their roots. Many are thysus mages but not all of the children of the moon awoke to the path that resonates with their roots.<br /> <br /> <b>Order tools</b>: Pelts, shamanic rituals and items that have resided in the shadow (at least one lunar cycle)<br /> <br /> <b>Initiation</b><br /> 1: Occult(The shadow)<br /> 2: High speech<br /> 3: Rote Specialties (Occult, Athletics and Brawl)<br /> 4: Shadow name (2 dot)<br /> 5: Familiar (4 dot) [spirit]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2909,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","user":"Mr.F.I.X.","date":".  Added what type of familiar 05-24-2016, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T15:53:28-07:00","id":898312,"title":"","content":"I don't have the book yet, so forgive any foolishness on my part when it comes to these.<br /> <br /> ~The Windrose Society<br /> Concept-A group of Nameless with roots in the Age of Discovery; I'm not sure what the limits are on the size of Nameless Orders, but my thoughts are that they have outposts all around the Western hemisphere, though they only have one place where they can be said to have genuine power in our realm, a port city in Portugal. Their focus is on exploring what they think of as the modern frontier, the strange worlds outside our own that Sleepers don't even know about, from the Hedge and Shadow to other, more obscure vistas.<br /> <br /> ~Project PROVIDENCE<br /> Concept- A small, brand new Order that's barely worth the name, it was recentky founded by a small cabal (which may or may not be an actual Cabal) within the American government who seek to cultivate a barrier against occult intrusion in the government, making up for their lack of lore with what resources they can siphon off the federal budget. When the occult intruders find out, they will not be pleased.<br /> <br /> ~Keepers of the Vault<br /> Concept: A fanatical but technically not Banisher Nameless that sacrifices magical items to keep a powerful and dangerous Abyssal entity bound. <br /> <br /> ~The Final Crusade<br /> Concept: A small Obrimos Banisher group that believes that Obrimos are the chosen of God and that other Paths are the result of foul demonic bargains, and thus must be destroyed. <br /> <br /> The City-Walkers <br /> Concept: A group of geomancer in [Major City, at least several hundred years old] who believe that said location is alive and that it's their duty to keep it healthy and strong. Focused on geomancy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T17:40:06-07:00","id":900509,"title":"","content":"A 2E Conversion of the Elemental Masteries. <hr /><br /> <b><u>Elemental Masteries</u></b><br /> As old as the Diamond Orders and the Seers, and perhaps predating either if some sects are to be believed, the Elemental Masteries are one of the most widespread of the Nameless Orders. The ancients who founded them had a very different understanding of the way the universe works. To them, abstract concepts could not be divorced from material being. It wasn\u2019t that elemental fire, for example, symbolized inspiration and courage. Fire literally was inspiration and courage. They were the same thing. If you saw a fire, you weren\u2019t looking at an embodiment of courage and inspiration, anger and destruction, you were looking directly at those things. It wasn\u2019t that elemental stone symbolized fertility, craftsmanship and creation. Stone was those things. The Elemental Legacies still teach this. By extension, they say, all things were all other things. Everything is part of a vast unity, a totality. Everything, every person, animal, object, thought and concept is part of the whole.<br /> <br /> <b>Order Tools: </b>Resonant Environments (raises their Yantra bonus by +1), Symbols of the Classical Elements<br /> <br /> (o) -- A Mage of the Elemental Masteries begins is first taught how to use the language of the universe to lend power into her spells, and receives the High Speech Merit for free. Most other initiates find the curse of Quiescence peeling away from their eyes, granting them the Sleepwalker Merit.<br /> <br /> (oo) -- As the initiate advances through the teachings of the Elemental Masteries, he learns to make himself more receptive to their secrets. He gains a dot in the Meditative Mind Merit.<br /> <br /> (ooo) -- While the Pentacle and the Seers tend to focus on mudras in their approaches to the Art, the Elemental Masteries emphasize the power that comes from personifying the elements. Mages gain either a dot in Occult or two dots in the Shadow Name Merit. By this point, they may already be approached by any of the Tamer Legacies for further instruction. Sleepwalkers who reach this level of initiation are instead counted on to serve as aides and minor leaders within the Order. They gain a dot in Occult, or two dots in the Retainer Merit instead.<br /> <br /> (oooo) -- Whether Awakened or Sleepwalker, an initiate who reaches this level of understanding gains greater insights into the inner truths of the universe. This is reflected by him receiving three dots in the Astral Adept Merit. Awakened practitioners who are are already Astral Adepts may instead develop three Rote specialties based on their primary element, while Sleepwalkers can gain the Banner-Bearer Merit at three dots. This tier is the highest which the latter can ever hope to attain.<br /> <br /> (ooooo) -- Only the Wise occupy the highest positions within the Order, and those who do reach this have learned at least the fourth Attainment within a Tamer Legacy. True Elemental Masters receive a soul stone that belonged to a deceased member of their Legacy. And whenever they use it to target a member of the Order at Sympathetic Range, they raise their effective Sympathetic Link with them by a number of steps equal to half their Status dots, rounded up. This is crucial to the Elemental Masteries' ability to coordinate together despite being separated by vast distances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 02-04-2017, 04:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T18:41:13-07:00","id":900537,"title":"","content":"The Whispered Hand is relatively young for a Nameless Order, and those they encounter often mistake them for idealistic Arrows or technophilic Libertines; their true origin is far less likely to earn them friends. <br /> <br /> There's an aging contingent at the higher echelons of the Iron Pyramid that still reject or fear the ever-evolving tools of the modern era, and only the Panopticon and upstart Pantechnicon seem to truly grasp their real potential. A small number of these technocrats saw the tide turn against them during the Arab Spring and rejected the chains they revered, breaking away to form a bright new Order that understands the magical potential of social media. For the Whispered Hand, the invisible network that binds people together across the gulf of space has more inherent worth than dusty tomes or gilded artifacts.<br /> <br /> The Hand's founding cabals are primarily focused in North Africa (primarily Egypt, where they keep a watchful eye on the new government), but they're reaching out across the globe, hoping to overthrow oppressive systems with the twin powers of the Supernal and the wireless. Of particular interest to them is China, where overwhelming censorship smacks of Seer manipulation.<br /> <br /> Order tools: smartphones, graffiti, symbols of anonymity and unity. As embarrassing as it may be, many in the Whispered Hand adopt the cartoonish masks adopted by Western anarchists and hacktivists.<br /> <br /> 1: A Socialize or Computers specialty in (Social Media).<br /> 2: A dot of the Contacts merits (Local Activists), reflecting Sleepers they hope to forge into tools of revolution.<br /> 3: One dot of the Computers skill. No Hand worth her salt gets by without a little bit of technical know-how.<br /> 4: A three dot Safe Place, reflecting a nearby safe house with its own source of electricity and internet access. The Whispered Hand understands that people too often 'disappear' when they make their voices heard.<br /> 5: Two dots of Occultation and one dot of the Shadow Name merit, reflecting a mystical persona they've grown that exists as an online presence that only seems to reach the right ears. The mage is difficult to pin down, but is on her way to become a symbol for rebellion.<br /> <br /> The Whispered Hand has been lucky so far, and their defection isn't known to the wider Iron Pyramid - yet. There are still incredibly bitter Panopticon and Pantechnicon loyalists in the nations that experienced the Arab Spring, and they would love nothing more than to bring the souls of these breakaways to their patron Exarchs in blazing chains. Potentially angering Seer factions further abroad will get them into trouble they aren't armed to defend themselves from (et alone overthrow) but they've yet to make political inroads with the Pentacle that they need to survive. Such negotiation might not be possible should their origins come to light.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 05-26-2016, 09:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T05:52:03-07:00","id":953767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/898221-2e-insert-nameless-orders-here?p=900537#post900537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Whispered Hand is relatively young for a Nameless Order, and those they encounter often mistake them for idealistic Arrows or technophilic Libertines; their true origin is far less likely to earn them friends.<br /> <br /> There's an aging contingent at the higher echelons of the Iron Pyramid that still reject or fear the ever-evolving tools of the modern era, and only the Panopticon and upstart Pantechnicon seem to truly grasp their real potential. A small number of these technocrats saw the tide turn against them during the Arab Spring and rejected the chains they revered, breaking away to form a bright new Order that understands the magical potential of social media. For the Whispered Hand, the invisible network that binds people together across the gulf of space has more inherent worth than dusty tomes or gilded artifacts.<br /> <br /> The Hand's founding cabals are primarily focused in North Africa (primarily Egypt, where they keep a watchful eye on the new government), but they're reaching out across the globe, hoping to overthrow oppressive systems with the twin powers of the Supernal and the wireless. Of particular interest to them is China, where overwhelming censorship smacks of Seer manipulation.<br /> <br /> Order tools: smartphones, graffiti, symbols of anonymity and unity. As embarrassing as it may be, many in the Whispered Hand adopt the cartoonish masks adopted by Western anarchists and hacktivists.<br /> <br /> 1: A Socialize or Computers specialty in (Social Media).<br /> 2: A dot of the Contacts merits (Local Activists), reflecting Sleepers they hope to forge into tools of revolution.<br /> 3: One dot of the Computers skill. No Hand worth her salt gets by without a little bit of technical know-how.<br /> 4: A three dot Safe Place, reflecting a nearby safe house with its own source of electricity and internet access. The Whispered Hand understands that people too often 'disappear' when they make their voices heard.<br /> 5: Two dots of Occultation and one dot of the Shadow Name merit, reflecting a mystical persona they've grown that exists as an online presence that only seems to reach the right ears. The mage is difficult to pin down, but is on her way to become a symbol for rebellion.<br /> <br /> The Whispered Hand has been lucky so far, and their defection isn't known to the wider Iron Pyramid - yet. There are still incredibly bitter Panopticon and Pantechnicon loyalists in the nations that experienced the Arab Spring, and they would love nothing more than to bring the souls of these breakaways to their patron Exarchs in blazing chains. Potentially angering Seer factions further abroad will get them into trouble they aren't armed to defend themselves from (et alone overthrow) but they've yet to make political inroads with the Pentacle that they need to survive. Such negotiation might not be possible should their origins come to light.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I love these, though I'd argue that the Praetorian Ministry does appreciate technology quite a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T04:41:58-07:00","id":959174,"title":"","content":"Watching 2<sup>nd</sup> season of <b>Penny Dreadful</b> ( especially episode 3 ) I got final inspiration to create truly witch sabbath Nameless Order. So here it is.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Nameless Order - Lovers of Devil</span></b><br /> For almost millennium, Church has accused many women and man of contacts with Devil and getting sorcery powers from this. Many Awakened were misunderstood because of it \u2013 to Christians what was Supernal has become Hell, spells became curses and High Speech of Atlantis was Devil\u2019s Tounge. Lovers of Devil are Nameless that embraced those accusations and worship Dark One as their patron. More, they really can summon things that anyone could only describe as demons from Hell.<br /> <br /> Awakened from Pentacle or Seers alike agree that Lovers have made in compact with some being from Lower Depths that want to spread sin and wickedness. Mysterium scholars call this dimension as Inferno, but any other can simply call it Hell. As now labeled as Left Hand practice, it lived for almost one thousand years on outskirts of Awakened communities. Most of new members were coming from Nameless that were left on their own \u2013 when they uncovered cursed Grimoire or relict of previous sabbath, Lovers come in compact with lower demons from this realm and form covens around it. Their patrons give them clues and advices to find other of their kind, forming loose alliance over whole countries or continents.<br /> <br /> <b>Order Tools:</b> Blood, sacrifice, orgies.<br /> <br /> <b>Initiation</b><br /> 1: Patron \u2013 Novice in coven need to make Pact with Patron of it, being able to communicate with Inferno demon by rituals.<br /> 2: High Speech ( as Devils Tongue )<br /> 3: Vice-Ridden ( CoD Rulebook )<br /> 4: Library (Occult) 3<br /> 5: Summoning \u2013 Highest witch in sabbath can summon it\u2019s Patron as instant action by connection it have with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T00:42:08-08:00","id":1042264,"title":"","content":"Need some help with two dots of Initiation..<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Nameless Order - Dreamspeakers</span></b><br /> Dreamspeakers Legacy is said to hail from various shamanistic traditions, connecting holy men with so called Dreamborns in Anima Mundi \u2013 gods of Dreamtime. This Nameless Order is template for those aboriginal cults that you still can found in heart of Africa, Australia, Oceania, North and South America. From Age of Exploration, Mysterium were doing extensive research on them, seeing some universal patterns in those primal communities, but most of them over throw people that were studying them and their \u2018white magic\u2019. When come Nameless War and many of those indigenous communities were endangered, future Dreamspeakers joined Nameless and later Free Council as Libertines. Still, there are enclosed communities in world that did not welcome both Diamond or Free Council and they stick to their own belief in Dreamborns.<br /> <br /> <b>Order Tools:</b> Admission of entheogen, Ritual dancing, ???<br /> <br /> <b>Initiation</b><br /> 1: High Speech Merit ( as Dreamborn Tales or incantations )<br /> 2: ???<br /> 3: ???<br /> 4: Astral Adept<br /> 5: Summoning \u2013 Highest shamans can summon their Dreamborn patron as instant action by connection it have with it. As powerful goetia, Dreamborns do not have Manifestations, so they linger in Twilight near shaman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T00:53:08-08:00","id":1042266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/898221-2e-insert-nameless-orders-here?p=1042264#post1042264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Need some help with two dots of Initiation..<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Nameless Order - Dreamspeakers</span></b><br /> Dreamspeakers Legacy is said to hail from various shamanistic traditions, connecting holy men with so called Dreamborns in Anima Mundi \u2013 gods of Dreamtime. This Nameless Order is template for those aboriginal cults that you still can found in heart of Africa, Australia, Oceania, North and South America. From Age of Exploration, Mysterium were doing extensive research on them, seeing some universal patterns in those primal communities, but most of them over throw people that were studying them and their \u2018white magic\u2019. When come Nameless War and many of those indigenous communities were endangered, future Dreamspeakers joined Nameless and later Free Council as Libertines. Still, there are enclosed communities in world that did not welcome both Diamond or Free Council and they stick to their own belief in Dreamborns.<br /> <br /> <b>Order Tools:</b> Admission of entheogen, Ritual dancing, ???<br /> <br /> <b>Initiation</b><br /> 1: High Speech Merit ( as Dreamborn Tales or incantations )<br /> 2: ???<br /> 3: ???<br /> 4: Astral Adept<br /> 5: Summoning \u2013 Highest shamans can summon their Dreamborn patron as instant action by connection it have with it. As powerful goetia, Dreamborns do not have Manifestations, so they linger in Twilight near shaman.</div> </div> </div> </div>The alredy existing benefits line up with Mystery Cult Initiation, and apparently mage-only, so I'll follow the suit and suggest one dot of the Dream Merit for the second rank, and the two-dot version of the Familiar Merit for the third rank (representing a Rank 1 Goetia who is a servant of the Dreamborn patron)<br /> <br /> The third Order Tool could be something related to Aboriginal culture, if this Nameless Order is culturally enclosed as you describe.<br /> <br /> Oh, and is it really okay for Dreamborn to be fully summoned that easily? I thought they were too big for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":".  grammar and details 02-02-2017, 03:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T17:24:07-08:00","id":1042692,"title":"","content":"I don't have it written up fully, but I did fun translate the final fantasy version of summoners. They're both a nameless order and a legacy which (attainment wise) is mechanically mostly taken from wyrdhamster's conversion of the Choir of Hashmallim crosschecked with the summonses book. I tinkered with the early attainments, but the whole idea is that Summoners are the ground level version of the Alienated. Summoners begin by earning a familiar, based on their Path. Each summoner makes pilgrimage to various sarira-like idols in order to commune with specific supernal beings with the desire to make a pact with them (also limited by Path). I tried to keep it with the feeling of an ancient Atlanta order while also being considered too wreckers and perhaps presumptuous to stand along with the other orders.<br /> <br /> Storyline wise, the nameless order is small. After a conflict long ago, the Summoner's order was officially considered left handed. Summoners try to maintain their lore, but over thousands of years, the true origins of the order and the mysterious primal entities they commune with are lost. there are legends--the mighty Ifrit is said to have been a harsh warlord who'd sacrificed his men but just as easily die himself for an idea, for example. But because summoners are already rare, and the Trials of the summoned monsters are harsh, there is very little firsthand knowledge amongst them, and almost all of it comes from the words of but a single Eidolon. While all ten of the eidolon are known by many names, not all have an active summoner to share their knowledge. indeed, some eidolon dream in sarira-temples lost in the mortal world and accessible only via the astral.<br /> <br /> A summoner's path often begins by goetic or animistic summoning and binding, swindling goblins into alliances, understanding angels, or necromancy. If another summoner mentors them, or if their soul connects to the summoner's path, they will be contacted by a familiar--an Obrimos is contacted by the thoughtforms of the holy familiar Carbuncle, acanthi are met with by the quiet and omnipresent Mogri, etc. This familiar is their envoy to the dreaming gods. Once they are initiated into the third attainment, they can challenge an Eidolon for the right to summon an avatar. Each has its own associated symbology, and no Summoner can summon a supernal Esper outside of their path unless they have Order Status 5 or are an archmaster. <br /> <br /> <br /> The benefits and drawbacks of an Avatar are why the legacy-order is considered left handed. while the summonses are quick to point out that an avatar is a mere ochemata reflected through the summoner, many conservative mages (especially Mysterious and Guardians) find the idea of such regular exposure of the supernal to the fallen as blasphemous. And they aren't wrong. avatars suffer when exposed to sleepers (and thus often react violently to them) and avatars do harm to sleeper souls. but the benefits are just as clear, as each Eidolon is vastly aware and full of lore, in addition to the infinite reach applied to spells cast by supernal beings. Even in their days first mastering a weak avatar, summoners can sacrifice dice pool for free reach. It is said that by the fourth and fifth legacy attainments that the summonses gain sudden and startling power. to this day, the mysterious still refuses to support any local summoners, referencing long forgotten wars in which summonses unleashed godly avatars that cost more lives than they were worth to finally contain them. the legendary wyrm king Bahamut is whispered to have single handedly destroyed a cityscape of magi. <br /> <br /> The order has a big secret that is the true reason it is considered illegal--like the seers of the throne, the division between archsummoner and summoned is not upheld. not only do the small handul of archsummoners directly train and aide their students, they also begin to teach them the basic cosmology of the imperial mysteries. They understand the world-beings of greater gods, they understand ochema, they understand the war of ascension and pax arcana. they are not taught the extent of imperial practices, nor involved in the petty vendettas or the invisible masters. they are not even taught how to reach the second horizon. however, there has never been an archsummoner who did not understand exactly what they were getting themselves into.<br /> <br /> Archmasters find themselves becoming friends and allies of the alien eidolon. they seek the lost and apocryphal bound and other esters. they all are Alienated, and speak of a Warring Triad.... three man made rank 9 beings, according to the lore, as an experiment in the time before. the three or four archsummoners active today whispered that oracles or exarchs created the warring triad as an experiment. as part of the omens of their numenon. because all say that the warring triad was killed by the exarchs, after the triad did the dirty work in the titanomachy, three ultimate summons that the exarchs unleashed to defeat the old gods..... if that is true, perhaps the warring triad are not dead, but instead a part of the massive tyranate.<br /> <br /> But that's just what a Mogri told me, and he was drunk on redcap bloodwine. summonses don't really exist, much less supernal gods tied to humans or a warring triad of superweapons employed during the titanomachy...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T23:12:20-08:00","id":1042833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/898221-2e-insert-nameless-orders-here?p=1042264#post1042264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Need some help with two dots of Initiation..<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Nameless Order - Dreamspeakers</span></b><br /> <br /> <b>Initiation</b><br /> 1: High Speech Merit ( as Dreamborn Tales or incantations )<br /> 2: ???<br /> 3: ???<br /> 4: Astral Adept<br /> 5: Summoning \u2013 Highest shamans can summon their Dreamborn patron as instant action by connection it have with it. As powerful goetia, Dreamborns do not have Manifestations, so they linger in Twilight near shaman.</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;Dream&quot; merit at one or two dots seems thematic. (p.101 MtA 2nd Edition) Though it needs Composure 3 and Wits 3 so that might be a bit restrictive. <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit\">21C Hermit</a></b> also suggested this Merit.<br /> <br /> An &quot;Astral Space&quot; Skill Specialty for Investigation or Occult skill might also fit as the first merit, moving &quot;High Speech&quot; to the second merit.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","name":"RBAWintrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T23:13:42-08:00","id":1042835,"title":"","content":"Are the Merits you get for Mistery Cult Initiation different for every member or all the same?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","name":"RBAWintrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T23:22:31-08:00","id":1042837,"title":"","content":"Dreamspeakers improved from Hermits and RBAWintrow comments write-up. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Nameless Order - Dreamspeakers</span></b><br /> Dreamspeakers Legacy is said to hail from various shamanistic traditions, connecting holy men with so called Dreamborns in Anima Mundi \u2013 gods of Dreamtime. This Nameless Order is template for those aboriginal cults that you still can found in heart of Africa, Australia, Oceania, North and South America. From Age of Exploration, Mysterium were doing extensive research on them, seeing some universal patterns in those primal communities, but most of them over throw people that were studying them and their \u2018white magic\u2019. When come Nameless War and many of those indigenous communities were endangered, future Dreamspeakers joined Nameless and later Free Council as Libertines. Still, there are enclosed communities in world that did not welcome both Diamond or Free Council and they stick to their own belief in Dreamborns.<br /> <br /> <b>Order Tools:</b> Admission of entheogen, Ritual dancing, ???<br /> <br /> <b>Initiation</b><br /> 1: High Speech Merit ( as Dreamborn Tales or incantations )<br /> 2: Dream 1 Merit<br /> 3: Familiar 2 Merit ( as servant to your Dreamborn patron )<br /> 4: Astral Adept Merit<br /> 5: Summoning \u2013 Highest shamans can summon their Dreamborn patron by connection it have with it. It works like Supernal Being summoning, only as powerful goetia, Dreamborns do not have Manifestations, so they linger in Twilight near shaman and do not lose Corpus or Mana from time spent in Twilight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T23:22:47-08:00","id":1042838,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Cult of Minerva</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Timeline:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Cult of Minerva rejected Catholicism and joined the de-Christianization efforts of the pagan (sleeper) Cult of Reason during the French Revolution. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Nickname - Minvervists</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* Occult specialty in Hellenistic Sorcery, which opens up deities as Hellenistic Path Tools when invoked or inscribed on amulets.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Acanthos</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Tyche, Ananke, the Fates, and Chronos.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mastigos</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Horus, Set, and Hathor. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Moros</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Anubis, Hades, Hephaestus. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Obrimos</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Hercules, Zeus, Thoth</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Thyrsos</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Sekhmet, Dionysus</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">** High Speech, which they refer to as Atlantean. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">*** Techne, but limited to the de-Christianized Greco-paganism of the Revolution.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">**** Astral Adept - for traveling to other countries to spread the Revolution. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">***** Access to a communal 3 dot Sanctum/Safe Place/Hallow. </span></span><br /> <br /> I used the Minervists in my 1814 Napoleonic Wars game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T23:49:13-08:00","id":1042846,"title":"","content":"Written for the Kingdom of Yamatai Dark Era I work on from time to time. <hr /><br /> <b><u>The Daughters of the Sun</u> (o to ooooo)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Sleepwalker or Awakened<br /> <b>Effect:</b> You are one of the few women who have been granted the honor to serve Himiko as a handmaiden and disciple. While your newfound position is heavy with risk and responsibility, you stand to gain much as you work to earn the Sun Queen's favor.<br /> <br /> <b>(o) </b>-- You have been named a Daughter of the Sun, and are now training to navigate the politics of Himiko's court. You gain the one-dot version Trained Observer.<br /> <br /> <b>(oo)</b> -- As a Sun Priestess, you are taught various subjects such as languages, etiquette, history and warfare. You gain either a free Specialty to one of the following Skills (Academics, Occult, Politics, Expression, or Socialize), or the Area of Expertise Merit tied to an appropriate Specialty.<br /> <br /> <b>(ooo)</b> -- You are a true initiate of Himiko, and have learned to discern supernatural influence whenever it manifests within your sight. You gain the Eye for the Strange Merit. Awakened members can choose instead to take the <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BxveHUKxwBU9ejlGcDYtN3hZTWs/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Keen Periphery or Supernal Taxonomy</a> Merit.<br /> <br /> <b>(oooo)</b> -- You have spent much time within the Sun Queen's Astral Realm, and have learned how to access it without the need for a place of power. You gain the Astral Adept Merit. This is the highest level of initiation for most Sleepwalkers.<br /> <br /> <b>(ooooo)</b> -- You are one of Himiko's favored servants, and it is likely that she will choose you to be her successor if you prove yourself worthy. Until then, the prestige of your position gives greater weight to your words and actions. You gain three dots to allocate between Inspiring, Cohesive Unit, and Small Unit Tactics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 02-03-2017, 05:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T15:33:01-08:00","id":1043189,"title":"","content":"I try to hammer general Tamers of Elements initiation spread. Would appreciate any help. <br /> <br /> Nameless Order - Elemental Masteries <br /> Tamers of Elements are said to be largest independent Nameless Order. Some say their dogmas of Paths being both spiritual and physical Elements are as old as civilization. Others point to Vinca culture and other neolithic societies remanents as signs of this idea. Truth is probably between them. Gamers are famous of their Legacies, but even non decided members commune with their Elements. Their practices are based on connecting particular Paths with physical Elements - for this correspondence see book Legacy: the Ancient. <br /> <br /> 1. Member can use physical Element of his Path as Environmental Yantra. <br /> 2. ??? <br /> 3.??? <br /> 4. - 5. - for those levels I thought about specific Tamers Merits - like Tamers of Fire would get Inspiring Merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T21:27:59-08:00","id":1043372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/898221-2e-insert-nameless-orders-here?p=1043189#post1043189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I try to hammer general Tamers of Elements initiation spread. Would appreciate any help. <br /> <br /> Nameless Order - Elemental Masteries <br /> Tamers of Elements are said to be largest independent Nameless Order. Some say their dogmas of Paths being both spiritual and physical Elements are as old as civilization. Others point to Vinca culture and other neolithic societies remanents as signs of this idea. Truth is probably between them. Gamers are famous of their Legacies, but even non decided members commune with their Elements. Their practices are based on connecting particular Paths with physical Elements - for this correspondence see book Legacy: the Ancient. <br /> <br /> 1. Member can use physical Element of his Path as Environmental Yantra. <br /> 2. ??? <br /> 3.??? <br /> 4. - 5. - for those levels I thought about specific Tamers Merits - like Tamers of Fire would get Inspiring Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Check out my take on the Elemental Masteries for ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T00:41:38-08:00","id":1043409,"title":"","content":"Was thinking about granting Skills Specialities related to philosophical element - maybe on second dot? <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/898221-2e-insert-nameless-orders-here?p=1043372#post1043372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Check out my take on the Elemental Masteries for ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean Legacies? As Legacies are more specialized then Nameless Orders on general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T01:24:16-08:00","id":1043415,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> <br /> <br /> Here is <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/898221-2e-insert-nameless-orders-here?p=900509#post900509\">my post</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T02:10:18-08:00","id":1043427,"title":"","content":"Ooh, I had been thinking about posting a thread like this myself; kudos to wyrdhamster for reviving this one.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <b>The Ashavan</b><br /> <br /> In ancient times there was an order of Persian willworkers known as the Karpani. Keepers of otherwise forgotten mystical traditions predating the revelations of Zarathustra, these magi were vilified by the prophet himself in the <i>G\u0101th\u0101s</i>, the oldest of the Zoroastrian scriptures. Accused of harming livestock, inflicting pains on the innocent, and influencing the good toward evil deeds, the Karpani vehemently opposed Zarathustra during his lifetime. Yet as time went on, the Karpani came to recognize the wisdom in the prophet's teachings, and by the time of Alexander's conquest of the Achaemenid Empire they had adopted much of the philosophy of the <i>Avesta</i> alongside their own occult practices, even if they never truly considered themselves followers of the Good Religion.<br /> <br /> <br /> In the great mystic melting-pot of the Hellenistic World, many of the Karpani were counted among the founders of the Diamond Orders, particularly the Guardians of the Veil and the Pancryptiates, while others, particularly among the more martially-inclined <i>Artestars</i>, would ultimately be seduced by the nascent Seers of the Throne. Yet those most faithful to the culture that birthed their order remained aloof from either group, their loyalties and interests lying with their sleeper kinsmen. Indeed, as conflicts flared between mages in the era of the Diadochi, the remaining independent Karpani turned their back on Awakened politics altogether. Most of these independent Karpani belonged to a moralistic faction known as the <i>Yashtipati</i>, &quot;masters of the <i>Yashts</i> (hymns)&quot;, but in time they adopted a new title for themselves: the <i>Ashavan</i>, meaning &quot;bearers of righteousness&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> For more than a thousand years, the Ashavan were among the most influential and widespread Nameless Orders in the world, albeit a particularly loosely-organized one. Opposing the excesses of the Seers and the Diamond Orders alike, they dedicated themselves to defending and serving their sleeper families and communities. Although ancient tradition forbade them from serving as priests themselves, they developed close ties with the Zoroastrian priesthood and used these connections to nearly monopolize the recruitment of those who awakened withing Zoroastrian congregations. In this manner they effectively dominated the magical landscape of Persia and neighboring lands through the Parthian and Sassanid eras, but the very sleeper connections that had allowed them to be so successful would prove their undoing.<br /> <br /> <br /> The rise of Islam didn't put an end to the influence of Zoroastrianism overnight, nor did it immediately spell the end for the Ashavan, but following the Arab conquest of the Sassanid empire both went into decline. In the case of the Ashavan, this decline was helped along by rival orders of magi, particularly the Seers of the Throne, who were quick to capitalize on the worst impulses of the Muslim ruling class in order to eliminate the Order and its sleeper allies. Never a truly unified power to begin with, the power of the Ashavan was soon broken, and Persia once more became the battleground of foreign magi.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yet just as Zoroastrianism survives to the present day, so too do the Ashavan. A tiny order mostly affiliated with conservative Parsi families in the Mumbai, though a few are thought to have emigrated with their sleeper kin to North America. Their efforts to avoid contact with other mages has given many the mistaken impression that they are hermits or &quot;Zoroastrian monks&quot; of some kind. This, however, reveals a fundamental misunderstanding of the faith; <i>active</i> moral participation in the world is a core element of Zarathustra's message, and the Ashavan embody this by dedicating themselves to spreading good thoughts, good words, and good deeds within their communities. This isn't to say they're all saints - they're as vulnerable to hubris as any magi - but the teachings of the Order attempt to instill a strong sense of moral duty in every new initiate. They tend to use their magic both subtly and sparingly, both in an effort to avoid hubris and because they believe that Paradox strengthens the Lie of Angra-Manyu and obscures the Truth of Ahura Mazda. Awakened of all paths are accepted by the Order, but Moros may fit less comfortably into their ranks, as any interaction with the dead is thought by the Ashavan to cause spiritual pollution.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Order Tools: </b>recitation of hymns or devotional poetry, ritually pure fire and water, white ritual vestments<br /> <br /> (o) - High Speech<br /> (oo) - Allies (o) related to a community member or members<br /> (ooo) - Rote Specialties (Empathy, Expression, Occult)<br /> (oooo) - Occultation (ooo)<br /> (ooooo) - not sure... I'm open to suggestions on this one","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 02-04-2017, 05:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T02:32:56-08:00","id":1043435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/898221-2e-insert-nameless-orders-here?p=1043427#post1043427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooh, I had been thinking about posting a thread like this myself; kudos to wyrdhamster for reviving this one.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <b>The Ashavan</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps the Astral Adept Merit or three dots in Dream? I imagine the Ashavan (and their Karpani predecessors) might perceive Astral Space as being where Asha is more strongly expressed than it is in the Fallen World?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T10:44:11-08:00","id":1043633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/898221-2e-insert-nameless-orders-here?p=1043435#post1043435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps the Astral Adept Merit or three dots in Dream? I imagine the Ashavan (and their Karpani predecessors) might perceive Astral Space as being where Asha is more strongly expressed than it is in the Fallen World?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmm... <i>To the Strongest</i> suggests that the Karpani associated goetia with the Daevas and considered ordinary dreams to be tied to <i>D</i><i>ruj</i>, but conversely that one could approach <i>Asha </i>in the deeper parts of the Astral through good thoughts. Based on that it seems like Astral Adept could make sense. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T07:50:15-08:00","id":1046764,"title":"","content":"Ooh, joining in on this! Currently, running a Chronicle set in Manila, which is home to various Nameless Mages and Orders.So here goes:<br /> <br /> Mga Inanak ni Hukluban (Children of Hukluban)<br /> A gathering of native Acanthi and Mastigoi who worship Hukluban, an ancient Filipino goddess of black magic and witchcraft. They practice ancient blood rites and tribal witchcraft, which Manila's Consilium would consider Left-Handed - if they didn't choose to look askance. Both Seers and Pentacle mages seek out Hukluban's Children for their gift of prophecy, and ability to weave fortune or misfortune.<br /> <br /> The Knife of Paradise (yep, took it from HtV)<br /> The Knife (an imperfect translation of 'kris', a local dagger-like sword) are a small group of Awakened who watch over Manila's Muslim quarter. Almost all have roots in the Consilia of Marawi and Zamboanga. Its leader is an Obrimos who parses gnostic language from the Qur'an. Explorers and scholars, they sometimes find common cause with the local Mysterium when their goals align.<br /> <br /> Vox Populi<br /> Vox Populi are modernist mages involved in Manila's vast call center industry. They see BPOs as a modern human phenomenon, and offshore sites as nexuses of information where they can study Sympathies. Not surprisingly, Mastigoi are the most respected within Vox Populi followed by Obrimoi.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4260-terpsichordean","name":"terpsichordean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4260_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T08:45:03-08:00","id":1046796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>terpsichordean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/898221-2e-insert-nameless-orders-here?p=1046764#post1046764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooh, joining in on this! Currently, running a Chronicle set in Manila, which is home to various Nameless Mages and Orders.So here goes:</div> </div> </div> </div>I really am curious if the Knife of Paradise has any connections with the Ascending Ones.<br /> <br /> The Vox Populi and the Children of Hukluban are equally interesting. And I do wonder what other Nameless Orders call your version of Metro Manila home.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}